085. 10.1098/rspb.2014.3085 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n27.Gibney ER, Nolan CM. Epigenetics and gene expression.\nHeredity (Edinb). 2010; 105:4–13. 10.1038/hdy.2010.54 [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n28.Rhodes T, Girman CJ, Savin RC, Kaufman KD, Guo S, Lilly FR, Siervogel RM, Chumlea WC. Prevalence of male pattern hair loss in 18-49 year old men.\nDermatol Surg. 1998; 24:1330–2. 10.1111/j.1524-4725.1998.tb00009.x [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n29.Krupa Shankar D, Chakravarthi M, Shilpakar R. Male androgenetic alopecia: population-based study in 1,005 subjects.\nInt J Trichology. 2009; 1:131–3. 10.4103/0974-7753.58556 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n30.Drewelies J, Hueluer G, Duezel S, Vetter VM, Pawelec G, Steinhagen-Thiessen E, Wagner GG, Lindenberger U, Lill CM, Bertram L, Gerstorf D, Demuth I. Using blood test parameters to define biological age among older adults: association with morbidity and mortality independent of chronological age validated in two separate birth cohorts.\nGeroscience. 2022; 44:2685–99. 10.1007/s11357-022-00662-9 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n31.Janssen F, Peeters A, Mackenbach JP, Kunst AE, and NEDCOM. Relation between trends in late middle age mortality and trends in old age mortality--is there evidence for mortality selection?\nJ Epidemiol Community Health. 2005; 59:775–81. 10.1136/jech.2004.028407 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n32.Reichert T, Chowell G, McCullers JA. The age distribution of mortality due to influenza: pandemic and peri-pandemic.\nBMC Med. 2012; 10:162. 10.1186/1741-7015-10-162 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n33.French National Institute for Demographic Studies (INED).\nAge and risk of mortality. 2018. from https://www.ined.fr/en/everything_about_population/graphs-maps/interpreted-graphs/age-risk-mortality/\n\n\n34.Kanherkar RR, Bhatia-Dey N, Csoka AB. Epigenetics across the human lifespan.\nFront Cell Dev Biol. 2014; 2:49. 10.3389/fcell.2014.00049 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n35.The dynamic epigenome.\nNat Struct Mol Biol. 2013; 20:258. 10.1038/nsmb.2534 [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n36.Dugué PA, Bassett JK, Joo JE, Jung CH, Ming Wong E, Moreno-Betancur M, Schmidt D, Makalic E, Li S, Severi G, Hodge AM, Buchanan DD, English DR, et al. DNA methylation-based biological aging and cancer risk and survival: Pooled analysis of seven prospective studies.\nInt J Cancer. 2018; 142:1611–9. 10.1002/ijc.31189 [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n37.Karouzakis E, Gay RE, Gay S, Neidhart M. Epigenetic deregulation in rheumatoid arthritis.\nAdv Exp Med Biol. 2011; 711:137–49. 10.1007/978-1-4419-8216-2_10 [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n38.Nemtsova MV, Zaletaev DV, Bure IV, Mikhaylenko DS, Kuznetsova EB, Alekseeva EA, Beloukhova MI, Deviatkin AA, Lukashev AN, Zamyatnin AA  Jr. Epigenetic Changes in the Pathogenesis of Rheumatoid Arthritis.\nFront Genet. 2019; 10:570. 10.3389/fgene.2019.00570 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n39.Oshima J, Sidorova JM, Monnat RJ  Jr. Werner syndrome: Clinical features, pathogenesis and potential therapeutic interventions.\nAgeing Res Rev. 2017; 33:105–14. 10.1016/j.arr.2016.03.002 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n40.Guastafierro T, Bacalini MG, Marcoccia A, Gentilini D, Pisoni S, Di Blasio AM, Corsi A, Franceschi C, Raimondo D, Spanò A, Garagnani P, Bondanini F. Genome-wide DNA methylation analysis in blood cells from patients with Werner syndrome.\nClin Epigenetics. 2017; 9:92. 10.1186/s13148-017-0389-4 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n41.Webb D, Roberts I, Vyas P. Haematology of Down syndrome.\nArch Dis Child Fetal Neonatal Ed. 2007; 92:F503–7. 10.1136/adc.2006.104638 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n42.Becht E, McInnes L, Healy J, Dutertre CA, Kwok IW, Ng LG, Ginhoux F, Newell EW. Dimensionality reduction for visualizing single-cell data using UMAP.\nNat Biotechnol. 2018. [Epub ahead of print]. 10.1038/nbt.4314 [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n43.Georgountzou A, Papadopoulos NG. Postnatal Innate Immune Development: From Birth to Adulthood.\nFront Immunol. 2017; 8:957. 10.3389/fimmu.2017.00957 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n44.Kumar BV, Connors TJ, Farber DL. Human T Cell Development, Localization, and Function throughout Life.\nImmunity. 2018; 48:202–13. 10.1016/j.immuni.2018.01.007 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n45.Eling N, Morgan MD, Marioni JC. Challenges in measuring and understanding biological noise.\nNat Rev Genet. 2019; 20:536–48. 10.1038/s41576-019-0130-6 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n46.Wilhelm-Benartzi CS, Koestler DC, Karagas MR, Flanagan JM, Christensen BC, Kelsey KT, Marsit CJ, Houseman EA, Brown R. Review of processing and analysis methods for DNA methylation array data.\nBr J Cancer. 2013; 109:1394–402. 10.1038/bjc.2013.496 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n47.Yong WS, Hsu FM, Chen PY. Profiling genome-wide DNA methylation.\nEpigenetics Chromatin. 2016; 9:26. 10.1186/s13072-016-0075-3 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n48.Sugden K, Hannon EJ, Arseneault L, Belsky DW, Corcoran DL, Fisher HL, Houts RM, Kandaswamy R, Moffitt TE, Poulton R, Prinz JA, Rasmussen LJ, Williams BS, et al. Patterns of Reliability: Assessing the Reproducibility and Integrity of DNA Methylation Measurement.\nPatterns (N Y). 2020; 1:100014. 10.1016/j.patter.2020.100014 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\n\n49.Lu AT, Fei Z, Haghani A, Robeck TR, Zoller JA, Li CZ, Lowe R, Yan Q, Zhang J, Vu H, Ablaeva J, Acosta-Rodriguez VA, Adams DM, et al. Universal DNA methylation age across mammalian tissues.\nNat Aging. 2023. [Epub ahead of print]. 10.1038/s43587-023-00462-6 [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar]\nAssociated Data\nThis section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article.\nSupplementary Materials\nSupplementary Figures\n\naging-15-205046-s001.pdf (1.5MB, pdf) \nSupplementary Data Excel\n\naging-15-205046-s002.xlsx (5MB, xlsx) \nData Availability Statement\nAll data sets used in this study are publicly available on NCBI’s GEO database, found at https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/.\nEquations\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(1)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(2)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(3)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(4)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(5)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(6)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(7)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(8)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(9)\n\n\n\nOpen in a new tab\nArticles from Aging (Albany NY) are provided here courtesy of Impact Journals, LLC\n\n                      \n\n                    \n                \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n            \n        \n    \n       \n              ACTIONS\n           \n               \n               \n                     \n                         \n                         View on publisher site\n                     \n               \n               \n               \n               \n                    \n                         \n                        PDF (2.5 MB)\n                    \n               \n               \n                \n               \n                   \n                       \n                       Cite\n                    \n               \n                \n               \n\n                        \n                            \n                            \n                            Collections\n                       \n               \n               \n                    \n                        \n                        Permalink\n                    \n                   \n\n\n    \n          PERMALINK\n          \n              \n              \n                  \n                  Copy\n              \n          \n    \n\n               \n           \n       \n     \n\n        \n            RESOURCES\n         